!! The Wave

''Composed by the controller'' from the two ratchets above (#/hearth-reader, #/shore-reader). The wave carries only what both readers signed; where they still part, it names the fork for the operator. Nothing here reads as a road row until the operator places it.

!!! Rulings ~ the operator, 2026-10-31 (talk-story)

<<~ moolelo held="the bridge-warden stands as a Kahu-chartered seat; herms remain the blind relay tier of Lararia and never carry a warden cap; build pressure rests ~ the pool lives as talk-story and design meme until after the founding proof; every lean of the floor approved (operator)">>
* ''The Votive'' retains bounty pools: each neighbor pours a gift to the warden marked for one question; many pledge, one seat writes. The answer lands in the Nexus's //working// wiki under the spirit's name and reaches canon only through `meme promote` with the seats' approval. A house-authored research spirit answers; the neighbor asks, never drives the model.
* ''The Johnson's Scribe'' retains the fixer's board: the pool pays only for a spirit that helps a neighbor shape a messy need into a clear ask. The board itself stays a credit-free `@crossroads` surface inside a chartered Nexus, known-user rung and above; the charter says the house brokers nothing.
* ''Clear in transit, sealed at rest'' (fork 2): the warden holds the bytes in memory, writes receipts only, keeps no body on disk; it //could// see, and by design never keeps.
* ''Tiered subscriptions, base free, plus open donations'' (fork 3): coin buys a membership in the house's product (A.1); mana stays an internal meter, never sold or redeemed as cash; gifts between neighbors move only earned or donated mana. Lineage to read: Boris Mann's open-org practice ~ CoSocial runs member tiers and its whole ledger in the open on Open Collective, with Fission once its fiscal host.
* ''The pool stands 18+'' (fork 4); the rest of the DreamNet stays open to younger members; the line reopens once the business org can carry the minors duty.
* ''The house's own cap shape'' (fork 5): the `cap-tier` meet plus an epoch caveat, checked at the warden, which spends every cap online. The cross-Nexus hop ~ whether another Nexus's warden honors this Nexus's cap ~ moves to treaty ground.
<<~/moolelo>>

!!! Signed Lines ~ both seats hold these

* ''The seat.'' The bridge-warden, a Kahu-chartered seat on the vessel holding the reach vault, alone reads a pour cap, meters the call, holds the counter and writes the receipt; the herm relays sealed bytes and sees none of it.
* ''The ledger.'' The Nexus Kahu realm owns the pool ledger (one owner per registry); the warden writes it; a face carries only its own receipts.
* ''The spend.'' Mana redeems only against house-authored spirits ~ fixed prompts, fixed tool surface ~ never a passthrough prompt box (the A.1 / D.4a line, as both readers read it; never legal advice).
* ''The season.'' A cap expires by epoch, advanced by a Kahu act; no wall clock decides.
* ''The ceiling.'' A ceiling binds per person, never per face, so a Persona split multiplies nothing.
* ''The mark.'' Every spirit-written line carries the spirit's name; every pour names "this leaves the island".

!!! Gates ~ nothing crosses these before they open

# ''License'' ~ Anthropic's written approval of the mana mechanism, once the business org stands. Until then the pool serves the operator's own house alone and takes no coin.
# ''W25'' ~ no third person's prompt crosses off-island while the bag plane leaks its creator.
# ''Age floor'' ~ the DreamNet's floor decides whether the minors guidelines bind.
# ''Charter'' ~ the house Nexus charters the warden seat before any neighbor pours.

!!! Wave One ~ the closed hearth (operator's island only)

# ''L1 · the warden and one cap.'' One reach-vault key, one signed pour cap `{ceiling, rank-max, epoch}`, a warden verb that checks, calls, receipts and decrements. ''First red:'' a call past the ceiling returns `pool-dry` and writes a refusal receipt; a replayed cap id refuses. ''Never:'' a key on a herm, a wall clock, a provider key for any face.
# ''L2 · cap shape and attenuation.'' A public-key token a holder narrows and a verifier checks offline, over the `cap-tier` meet. ''First red:'' a child cap wider in rank or ceiling than its parent fails; a sixth hop fails. ''Never:'' settle the token family in code before the operator rules it.
# ''L3 · the season rite.'' One Kahu act advances the pool epoch and retires the season's caps. ''First red:'' a cap from epoch N fails after the act at N+1, no timer running. ''Never:'' expire on duration; refund on retirement.
# ''L4 · the hearth-fire measure.'' Price the cache on the house's own use for two weeks against Shore-Reader's table. ''First red:'' a repeated question over an unchanged wiki CID logs a hit; a changed CID logs a miss. ''Never:'' cache across faces; log a prompt body; put a private page in a shared prefix.

''Order:'' L1 first; L2 and L4 beside each other; L3 after L2.

!!! Wave Two ~ still closed, after wave one lands

# ''L5 · the dreaming queue.'' Ask now, or wake to the answer at half price. ''First measure:'' turnaround and a receipt that lands causal and clockless. ''Never:'' promise a wall-clock dawn; leave a batch job hanging across the epoch that retires its cap.
# ''L6 · the double-spend probe.'' A hired adversary tries to spend one bearer note twice offline. ''First red:'' two redemptions yield one `done` and one `already-spent` (the `veil-vouch` nullifier).
# ''L7 · the elder's scribe.'' The first house-authored spirit: an operator-chosen oral history, transcribed into the wiki with a consent record. ''First measure:'' the speaker reads back a sample and names the error rate. ''Never:'' a third party's voice before W25 closes and a consent step stands.

!!! Held Back

* ''Incense'' ~ waits on the `admission-price` vouch-ledger wiring; then a closed group of 10 to 20 trusted people and one hired farmer (Shore-Reader's lane E).
* ''Gift and coin'' ~ wait on the license; gift moves only earned or donated mana.
* ''Narrow pilots, later waves'' ~ the civic clerk (citations only, never what the law allows); the mediator (a drafting aid to a human facilitator inside talk-story and hoike).
* ''Deferred'' ~ the crossroads interpreter, storm mode, the Temple tier.
* ''Retained by reframe'' ~ bounty pools as the Votive, the fixer's board as the Johnson's Scribe (#/the-wave rulings); craft and kin aid folds into the clerk.

!!! Forks for the Operator

Forks 1 to 6 closed by the operator's rulings above. Still open: the in-person question ~ does the Johnson's Scribe's board ever help neighbors meet offline, or stay with online help alone?

