!! Muse's Takes ~ the open dish (agreed by the operator, research owed)

Born on the talk-story floor of 2026-10-31; the operator agreed with all seven and asked for more research (#/open-org-lineage, #/mana-scrip). Each pushback from the house rides beneath its take.

# ''The Temple as fiscal host.'' The business org stands as the first Temple: it holds the bank account, the provider agreement and the legal duty //for// Crossroads Nexuses too small to carry them, the way Fission hosted CoSocial until CoSocial stood alone. A Nexus graduates to independence.
#* //Stranger:// the Temple turns into the civic form of the causal-island boundary ~ test it against "share substrate, not sovereignty" lest it quietly turn sovereign.
# ''An open dish, an open bowl.'' The Kahu realm's pool ledger reads public to the Nexus ~ every pour, tier, donation and season tide ~ as CoSocial runs its books on Open Collective; receipts aggregate, prompts never appear. The Nexus's glass shows the dish level as ambient glow; neglect flickers.
#* //Council:// a small Nexus's ledger could unmask who poured ~ open books show amounts by tier and season, never by face, unless a pourer signs.
# ''Tiers as offerings.'' Incense (the free base, the floor that never closes) · grain (member) · wine (maintainer) · garland (an organization, one share). A higher tier buys more pour, never more vote.
# ''The season rite as the assembly.'' The pool's epochs take the five Discordian seasons ~ Chaos, Discord, Confusion, Bureaucracy, Aftermath ~ each advanced by a Kahu act; Aftermath holds the open-books review and sets the next tide.
# ''The smoke rises (demurrage).'' Unspent mana rises back to the Temple dish at a season's turn (Gesell, Wörgl): hoarding stops paying.
#* //Advocate:// a member may mark a votive before the turn, so saving for a purpose survives and only hoarding evaporates.
# ''The Votive flywheel.'' Each Votive answer promoted to canon joins the Nexus's cached hearth-fire prefix; a Nexus that answers its votives openly lowers its own cost of asking.
# ''A corner for Eris.'' A small share of each season's tide forms a Discord tithe, granted to a votive the oracle's blind throw picks ~ funding the question nobody voted for.

