!!! Where Boris Mann stands now

* ''Roles.'' His about page (modified 2026-04-06) lists: Ink & Switch COO, half-time; the other half on atproto community and ecosystem; CoSocial member; DWebYVR organizer; Z-Space director; advisor to Cosmik Network and Gander. SOURCED (https://bmannconsulting.com/about). The Ink & Switch line rests on that page alone; two searches found no outside confirmation.
* ''Fission.'' Fission's blog says the company wound active operations down by the end of May 2024, its identity, data and compute protocols staying open source. SOURCED (https://fission.codes/blog/). A people-profile lists Mann as co-founder and CEO from May 2019 to April 2024. SOURCED (https://village.ai/person/boris-mann-NTgxMDMyMDcy). The CoSocial fiscal-host handoff (July 2024) comes from the operator's earlier search, not re-read here.
* ''Site.'' His journal now lives at boris.mann.ca; recent entries (Oct 2026) cover AI-grown personal code and notes on atproto PDS tooling. SOURCED (https://bmannconsulting.com, via fetch). No essay on open finances surfaced. SOURCED-ABSENT.
* ''Now page'' (modified 2026-07-05): Berlin for DWeb Camp 2026 and Local-First Conf; AtmosphereConf 2026 follow-ups and 2027 planning; Ink & Switch Lab Day; an 18-month ARIA UK grant; the ZAI local-AI hardware project "moving toward funding"; the Atmosphere Community Co-Op "being formed". SOURCED (https://bmannconsulting.com/now).

!!! CoSocial ~ the books in the open

* ''Ledger.'' Open Collective lists Member at $50 CAD a year (one Mastodon account, an AGM vote), Maintainer at $250, Organization at $50 under $100,000 revenue and $250 above, a $50 one-time gift membership, and custom gifts. It shows balance $33,430 CAD, income $59,786, disbursed $26,356, estimated annual budget $16,020. SOURCED (https://opencollective.com/cosocial). The page names no fiscal host today. SOURCED.
* ''The $10 share.'' No page read this session mentions a $10 share; October 2026 entries show three flat $50 Member contributions. SOURCED (same URL). The pool should treat "$50 flat" as the current tier and the share as unconfirmed; INFERRED that an earlier bylaw or sign-up page carried a share. The join page (https://join.cosocial.ca/sign-up/) holds the answer; this reader never opened it.
* ''Governance.'' The 3rd AGM ran 2025-10-30: members approved the financial statements and a new growth strategy, changed three Rules, and elected two directors; the page states "100% of our revenue comes from membership fees and contributions". SOURCED (https://join.cosocial.ca/author/dawn). Minutes and the report package sit on a members-only Discourse. SOURCED. Mann sits on no 2025-2026 board list. SOURCED (same page); he calls himself a member. SOURCED (https://bmannconsulting.com/about).
* ''Cost drivers.'' Infrastructure stands as the largest expense; the co-op moved to Canadian hosts by end of 2025 to cut it, and reserves cover migration. SOURCED (same AGM page).

!!! Fiscal hosting, practised

